  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 140 AM EST Wed Nov 25 2026\n\n- Only Minor Weather-Related Michigan Travel Problems Expected\n\nA full latitude trough across the central CONUS will cut off from\nthe northern stream with the upper low and large sfc cyclone\ntapping both Gulf and Atlantic moisture as it moves northeast up \nthe Appalachians by the end of the week. The northwest precip\nshield, associated with an area of mid level frontogenesis, will\nbring rain on Thursday with the potential for some wet snow mixing\nin Thursday night.\n\nSince the low is cut off from the northern stream, there is a \nlimited push of cold air with surface temperatures near or above\nfreezing during the bulk of the precip. Model soundings from the\nGFS show the wet bulb zero height near the surface Thursday night\ninto Friday morning near and north of I-96, where there could be \nsome minor impacts to travel if wet snow accumulates/freezes on\nroads. \n\nThe precip winds down on Friday as the trowal/mid-level f-gen \ntranslates east and is replaced by shortwave ridging before a \nnorthern stream shortwave trough arrives late in the weekend. Cold\nair is once again limited but wet snow could mix in by Sunday\nnight.",
